1
00:00:00,002 --> 00:00:08,002
Roughly 70% of outages come from changes (Site Reliability Engineering, Google). Two deploys land in the same minute. Which one broke checkout?

2
00:00:08,002 --> 00:00:11,994
Checkout is failing and several deploys are in the window. Could D-rec-12 be the cause? Ask FalkorDB for a causal path to checkout (Q-GATE-1), read-only.

3
00:00:11,994 --> 00:00:20,000
No path, no claim: FalkorDB returns no causal path from D-rec-12 to checkout (0 rows), so it cannot be blamed.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,003
How it got here: a crew of least-privilege agents (9 steps · 5 specialists). Every step is a record in the graph: who claimed it, what it ran, who it handed to.

5
00:00:32,003 --> 00:00:44,001
D-email-88 shipped in the same minute and has a path. But algo.maxFlow says it can carry only 0.0200 of the 0.2433 needed. Rejected.

6
00:00:44,001 --> 00:00:52,380
The proof path, lit edge by edge: D-pay-417 → payment → checkout.

7
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:56,001
Why do you believe this? Provenance from the verdict back to the tool calls and agents that produced each piece of evidence (4 evidence · 5 calls · 2 agents), every arrow a stored edge.

8
00:00:56,001 --> 00:01:01,000
Smallest containment: cut payment
→
checkout, payment
→
raw.raw_orders (algo.maxFlow min-cut). A what-if on a GRAPH.COPY branch checks it first: contains.

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Who fixes it: Quinn Lindqvane (p-017) first, ranked by algo.HarmonicCentrality over who wrote this code and fixed past outages here.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,180
Choosing isn't approving: the server first renders the exact diff, the PR body and the plan hash.

11
00:01:10,180 --> 00:01:13,797
Approve this exact action, bound to plan hash d1354eca56f9: if the plan changes, the server refuses it.

12
00:01:13,797 --> 00:01:25,624
Approved: the one write tool opens the pull request, then VERIFY checks it through a second channel.

13
00:01:25,624 --> 00:01:32,980
APPLIED: GitHub main re-read and telemetry back in band. Write-back verified 7/7: RESOLVED, and the incident becomes memory.

14
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:36,617
A real pull request (#4), merged after two-step approval and verified through a second channel: APPLIED.

15
00:01:36,617 --> 00:01:41,683
Break it: take one edge out of a GRAPH.COPY of the graph and run the product again.

16
00:01:41,683 --> 00:01:41,867
Take a graph edge away and the decision changes (outcome: CONFIRMED → UNKNOWN_ESCALATED). The graph is load-bearing.

17
00:01:41,867 --> 00:01:43,721
Before the next deploy: the same graph scores the risky pull request.

18
00:01:43,721 --> 00:01:48,136
Preflight verdict: block. It contradicts ADR-012, ADR-013. The same graph that explained the outage gates the next change.

19
00:01:48,136 --> 00:01:48,193
Reversal guard: a PR that puts back what ADR-009 decided, which the team replaced with ADR-021, is named with the evidence (advisory; the verdict is unchanged).

20
00:01:48,193 --> 00:01:49,953
The company brain: who owns, knows and decided what.

21
00:01:49,953 --> 00:02:00,078
It answers citing only nodes its own queries returned (citation guard), and draws the answer as a graph.

22
00:02:00,078 --> 00:02:07,227
Right verdict on the scenario suite (24 trials): Faultline 100%; telemetry only 62.5%, vector similarity 25%, naive recency 0%. FalkorDB switched off confirms 0 causes.

23
00:02:07,227 --> 00:02:14,421
Confidently blaming the wrong change: Faultline 0%; telemetry only 20%, vector similarity 60%, naive recency 100%.

24
00:02:14,421 --> 00:02:21,620
Take FalkorDB's algorithms away: correct verdicts on 100 held-out worlds fall from 100 to 80 without algo.maxFlow, 76 without algo.SPpaths, 56 without both; confident wrong blames stay at 0.

25
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:28,814
Context for any agent, unrelated deploys crowding the window: the true cause ranks far higher in the graph's context pack (MRR 0.66) than in vector RAG (0.42) or by recency (0.08).

26
00:02:28,814 --> 00:02:36,979
The live deployment, measured over HTTPS: right cause 5/5, verified APPLIED 5/5; alert to RESOLVED p50 2,719 ms.

27
